/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL003 -- THE FROZEN SAMPLING RULE for the DEVELOPED-REGION DIAGNOSTIC.

  These two cell zones are NOT the gate.  The GATE is the inlet-to-outlet
  pressure difference read from the two patch `surfaceFieldValue` monitors in
  system/controlDict, exactly as the manual defines the compared quantity
  ("pressure difference between inlet and outlet", p. 19).

  These zones support the DECLARED DIAGNOSTIC of PREREGISTRATION.md section 3.3:
  the fully-developed axial pressure gradient, from which the friction factor
  actually realised by the turbulence model is recovered as

        f_dev = (dp/dx) * D / (0.5 rho U^2)

  This isolates the turbulence model's wall friction from (i) the entrance
  excess that the uniform inlet BC introduces and (ii) the Moody-chart read
  that the manual's printed target rests on.  It can NEVER change the gate
  verdict; it is printed beside it.

  Both slabs are 0.04 m long (10 D) and SYMMETRIC about their nominal station,
  so a volume average of a locally linear p returns the value at the station
  centre to second order.  Stations:

      slabA  centred x = 1.00 m  (250 D from inlet; the turbulent entrance
                                  length 4.4 Re^(1/6) D = 0.08608400083579049 m
                                  = 21.52 D ends at x = 0.086 m, so slabA is
                                  more than 11 entrance lengths downstream)
      slabB  centred x = 1.80 m  ( 50 D upstream of the fixedValue outlet, so
                                  the outlet pressure BC cannot contaminate it)

      separation SLAB_DX = 0.80 m = 200 D, fixed in grade_vmfl003.py.

  At the COARSEST level (NX = 250, dx = 0.008 m) each slab holds 5 axial cells
  x NR radial cells; at the finest (NX = 1000, dx = 0.002 m) it holds 20 x NR.
  Neither can be empty -- and run_vmfl003.sh REFUSES to start the solver if
  topoSet leaves either zone empty, and grade_vmfl003.py REFUSES (exit 2) if the
  `# Cells` header of either volFieldValue output is absent or 0.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      topoSetDict;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

actions
(
    {
        name    slabACells;
        type    cellSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToCell;
        box     (0.98 -1 -1) (1.02 1 1);
    }
    {
        name    slabA;
        type    cellZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  setToCellZone;
        set     slabACells;
    }

    {
        name    slabBCells;
        type    cellSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToCell;
        box     (1.78 -1 -1) (1.82 1 1);
    }
    {
        name    slabB;
        type    cellZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  setToCellZone;
        set     slabBCells;
    }
);

